That changes it: `Object.freeze()` is shallow. It freezes only the object's own properties—you can't reassign `cfg.db` to a different object. But `cfg.db` itself is not frozen, so `cfg.db.host = 'y'` mutates the nested object without error.

To freeze deeply, you'd need a recursive freeze:

```javascript
function deepFreeze(obj) {
  Object.freeze(obj);
  Object.values(obj).forEach(val => {
    if (typeof val === 'object' && val !== null) deepFreeze(val);
  });
  return obj;
}
```

Then `deepFreeze(cfg)` blocks both `cfg.db = ...` and `cfg.db.host = ...`.
